From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy Ritger <aritger@nvidia.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 17:16:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] nvkms: Move nvHsAllocDevice() before nvAllocLutSurfacesEvo()

From a patch Andy Ritger posted on NVIDIA's tracker for testing against
615.78.08, for the display freeze with nvidia-modeset spinning in
nvWriteGpEntry() <- PrefetchHelperSurfaceEvo() <- nvDIFRPrefetchSurfaces().
His post gave no description; the rest of this message is our reading of
the code.

AllocLutSurfaceEvoInVidmem() gives a LUT surface its GPU mapping with
nvHsMapSurfaceToDevice(), and says the mapping exists for DIFR prefetch.
That function returns 0 while pDevEvo->pHsDevice is NULL, and the LUT
surfaces were allocated before nvHsAllocDevice(), so the base, output and
default LUTs always had gpuAddress 0. nvDIFRPrefetchSurfaces() prefetches
them on every pass that gets that far, so stock code launched a copy from
GPU VA 0 and timed out with FAIL_CE_HW_ERROR, leaving GPFIFO entries behind.

Our lazy GPU map commit already refuses address 0 and reports the surface as
not prefetchable, so this stack doesn't launch that copy, but a prefetch pass
could never succeed either. With the mappings in place it can, so DIFR may
now actually engage at idle.

nvHsAllocDevice() only needs pNvKmsOpenDev and the push device, both set up
earlier. Teardown already frees the LUT surfaces before nvHsFreeDevice(), so
the new mappings are unmapped while the device still exists.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-evo.c | 10 +++++-----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-evo.c b/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-evo.c
index 34739096..66577ad9 100644
--- a/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-evo.c
+++ b/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-evo.c
@@ -9059,6 +9059,11 @@ NVDevEvoPtr nvAllocDevEvo(const struct NvKmsAllocDeviceRequest *pRequest,
         goto done;
     }
 
+    if (!nvHsAllocDevice(pDevEvo, pRequest)) {
+        status = NVKMS_ALLOC_DEVICE_STATUS_FATAL_ERROR;
+        goto done;
+    }
+
     if (!nvAllocLutSurfacesEvo(pDevEvo)) {
         nvEvoLogDev(pDevEvo, EVO_LOG_ERROR,
             "Failed to allocate memory for the display color lookup table.");
@@ -9083,11 +9088,6 @@ NVDevEvoPtr nvAllocDevEvo(const struct NvKmsAllocDeviceRequest *pRequest,
         goto done;
     }
 
-    if (!nvHsAllocDevice(pDevEvo, pRequest)) {
-        status = NVKMS_ALLOC_DEVICE_STATUS_FATAL_ERROR;
-        goto done;
-    }
-
     if (!pDevEvo->displaylessHw && !nvInitHdmiLibrary(pDevEvo)) {
         status = NVKMS_ALLOC_DEVICE_STATUS_FATAL_ERROR;
         goto done;
